# MadGraph5 batch script: g g > h NP<=1
# in SMEFTsim_topU3l_MwScheme (UFO v3.0.2), restricted by restrict_vg_cHGtil.dat.
#
# Why this exact process:
#   The same process with O_HGtil switched on beside O_HG: the CP-odd vertex
#   carries VVS1/VVS2, whose structure is `Epsilon(1,2,-1,-2)*P(-2,2)*P(-1,1)`.
#   The two contributions do not interfere in the helicity-summed |M|^2 (the
#   epsilon flips sign between the two gluon-helicity configurations and the
#   interference cancels), so this row's evidence for the epsilon sign is the
#   per-helicity AMP() table, not the cross section -- which is the reason the
#   amplitude gate compares per helicity per diagram at all.
#
#   2 -> 1 at fixed beams -- see bbx_to_h_identity for what that costs.
#
# The model path is repo-relative to the vendored UFO; build.sh rewrites it to
# the work-area copy it stages under output/models/, which is where the
# vg_* restrict cards of validation/madgraph/cards/smeft/ are placed. Both
# generators therefore prune vertices from the same card.
#
# `display interactions` prints the count MadGraph's own interaction splitting
# arrives at (one interaction per coupling-order tuple, import_ufo.add_interaction)
# into the build log, which is where extract_interactions.py reads it from.
#
# Orders are explicit because SMEFTsim gives NP hierarchy 99: MadGraph's default
# WEIGHTED bound would drop every diagram carrying a Wilson coefficient.
import model validation/ufo/SMEFTsim_topU3l_MwScheme_UFO-vg_cHGtil
display interactions
generate g g > h NP<=1
output gg_to_h_cpodd -nojpeg
launch
set lpp1 0
set lpp2 0
set ebeam1 62.545
set ebeam2 62.545
set use_syst False
done
